{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-a8-partition-function-identity","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:a8-partition-function-identity","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of a8 partition function identity","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-a-8-partition-function-identity"],"text":"a8-partition-function-identity-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:a8-partition-function-identity\"></a><p><strong>Proof.</strong> Coefficient-by-coefficient match in descending order of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code>-power:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Power of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code></th>\n<th>Coefficient in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a_8</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(n)</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 5 - k</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X^4</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(1) = 1</code> (match)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X^3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(2) = 2</code> (match)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 2</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X^2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(3) = 3</code> (match)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 3</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X^1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(4) = 5</code> (match)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 4</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X^0</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">7</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p(5) = 7</code> (match)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 5</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Each coefficient is the exact value of the integer partition\nfunction at the corresponding index. The identity is checked in\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[X]</code> by <code>ring</code> after expanding\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sum_{n=1}^{5}</code> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}</code>. ∎</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/a8-partition-function-identity-proof.md","heading":"Proof"}
